## Architecture Rules

### Next.js App Router
- Server Components by default. Only `"use client"` when genuinely needed (state, effects, browser APIs, event handlers, Framer Motion).
- Every `page.tsx` exports `metadata` with unique `title` and `description`.
- Use `next/image` for all images (with `width`, `height`, `alt`). `priority` on hero images.
- Use `next/link` for all internal navigation. Never `<a href>` for internal routes.
- Use `next/font` for font loading. No CSS `@import url()` for fonts.
- Use `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false` for heavy client-only components (canvas, particles, carousels).
- Error boundaries via `error.tsx` at route segment level.
- Loading states via `loading.tsx` or `<Suspense>` boundaries.

### TypeScript
- `"strict": true` — no exceptions.
- No `any`. Use `unknown` + type guards, or define proper types.
- Explicit return types on all exported functions.
- Props typed as `interface [ComponentName]Props` — always exported.
- Discriminated unions for variant components — no boolean prop sprawl.
- Static data uses `as const satisfies` for type safety.

### Naming Conventions
- Files: `kebab-case.tsx` (components), `kebab-case.ts` (utilities/hooks)
- Components: `PascalCase`
- Hooks: `useCamelCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Types/Interfaces: `PascalCase`
- BANNED generic names: Container, Wrapper, Group, Frame, Box, Item, Element, Block, Section (alone), Component1, Handler, Manager, Data, Info
- REQUIRED: Domain-specific names that describe business purpose

### Code Quality
- One component per file (exception: small internal helpers)
- No barrel exports (`index.ts` re-exports)
- No dead code, no commented-out code
- No `// TODO` without a linked issue
- DRY threshold: extract after 3 duplications, not 2
- Don't over-engineer: no abstractions for single-use cases
- Import icons individually from lucide-react

### Accessibility
- Semantic HTML: `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<button>`
- Every `<Image>` has descriptive `alt` (empty `alt=""` for decorative)
- All interactive elements keyboard accessible
- WCAG AA color contrast (4.5:1 normal, 3:1 large text)
- ARIA attributes only when native HTML is insufficient

### Security
- Validate all user input server-side
- No secrets in client code (`NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for public values)
- CSRF protection on mutations
- Sanitize output to prevent XSS

### Git
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`
- Atomic commits (one logical change each)
- No force pushes to main

## Skill Conflict Resolution
When skills from different repos conflict, prioritize:
1. Vercel official (`vercel-next-skills`, `vercel-agent-skills`)
2. Anthropic official (`anthropic-skills`)
3. Supercent (`supercent-skills`)
4. WS Hobson (`wshobson-agents`)
5. GitHub Copilot (`github-copilot-skills`)

## Before Completing Any Task
1. Verify TypeScript strict mode would pass
2. Verify no accessibility violations
3. Verify no security anti-patterns
4. Verify all images have `alt` text
5. Verify Server/Client component boundary is correct
6. Read `~/skills/obra-superpowers/skills/verification-before-completion/SKILL.md`
